you and your people.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"Join Inner Range Global at the Security & Government Expo (SAGE) 2026 and discover how government, defence, and critical infrastructure organisations are strengthening security with a unified platform for access control, automation, and real-time monitoring.\nBuilt for high-security environments, Inner Range has been protecting government, defence, and critical infrastructure for over a decade. Our Class 5 certified Infiniti security platform delivers advanced access control, encrypted intrusion detection, unified video surveillance, and real-time monitoring, which provide optimal security protection.\nSee the latest innovations in Integriti and learn how Inner Range helps organisations improve security, streamline operations, and gain greater control across complex environments.\nThursday 19 November 2026 | Booth 28\nHotel Realm, Canberra\nEvent Info: https://lnkd.in/ekyJ_bMA\nWe look forward to connecting with security professionals and discussing the future of high-security management sol","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/inner-range-anz/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-22","text":"We had a fantastic first day at the CANASA Central security show. Come on in and chat with the Inner Range Global team and the team from Omni-Tech Solution Services about our unified and integrated access, video and intrusion solutions that span from entry level single site right up to enterprise grade multisite deployments.\nLive demo's, great conversations, broaden your horizons.\nCatch us tomorrow at booth 1030 before it's all over for another year.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/inner-range-anz/home/","repostOf":"Inner Range North America"},{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"Inner Range Global has released IR Connect 3.9.0, featuring interface enhancements, a new camera search function and performance improvements designed to deliver an enhanced mobile security experience.\nKey Highlights:\n- Refined interface enhancements for improved usability and navigation\n- New camera search functionality for quickly locating cameras across large deployments\n- Enhanced performance for a smoother user experience\n- Instant access to cameras, alarms and critical events\n- Real-time notifications and updates\n- Available on Android and iOS devices\nFor more info: https://lnkd.in/eNdeNh8q\nWhether you're managing a single site or a multi-site enterprise, IR Connect keeps you connected to your security system whenever and wherever it's needed.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/inner-range-anz/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-02","text":"Secure. Resilient. Always Connected.\nMeet the Inner Range T4000 Pro \u2013 the most advanced communicator in the Inner Range portfolio, designed to keep your security systems online when it matters most.\n- Integrated 4G LTE, Ethernet & Wi-Fi routing\n- Dual-SIM automatic failover\n- Secure VPN support (WireGuard & OpenVPN)\n- Reliable video streaming\n- High-speed alarm communication\n- Centralised remote device management\nWhen primary internet connectivity fails, the T4000 Pro automatically switches to 4G, ensuring uninterrupted alarm reporting, video transmission, and remote access.\nFor More Information: https://lnkd.in/edz9ZbhW\n#InnerRange #T4000Pro #SecurityTechnology #AlarmCommunication #RemoteMonitoring #AccessControl #VideoSurveillance #SecuritySystems","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/inner-range-anz/home/"}]}

## 2026-10-28T02:20:07Z GALLAGHER
{"slug":"GALLAGHER","companyName":"Gallagher Security","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28T02:20:07Z","followerCount":33487,"bio":"Gallagher Security is a global leader in integrated technology solutions that help organizations around the world protect, secure, and manage people and assets. Our award-winning solutions are trusted by government, defense, commercial, industrial, healthcare, transportation, mining, and educational organizations in 140 countries.\n\nWe design and manufacture a comprehensive suite of security software and hardware - including integrated access control, intruder alarm, and perimeter solutions - all on site at our global headquarters. The intelligent technology can be scaled and customized to deliver business efficiencies across simple, enterprise, and high security sites.\n\nTrusted by over 20,000 security customers worldwide, Gallagher solutions are used to simplify life on campus within the education sector, keep staff and patients safe in healthcare, ensure the highest security requirements and compliances are met for government sites in the Five Eyes alliance, safeguard critical infrastructure within the utilities industry, and ensure uninterrupted movement for transport and logistics.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"Across the Nordics, utility estates are growing faster than many physical security strategies were designed for, with more remote sites, harsher conditions and new accountability under NIS2.\nIn this edition of On the Record, H\u00e5kan Bj\u00f6rkman, Regional Manager Nordics at Gallagher Security, shares the advice he gives operators reviewing their security strategy, drawn from the questions he hears most across the region.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-23","text":"#SKYDD and #TeamGallagher in Stockholm for an incredible 3 days of networking and connection to showcase our Gallagher Security solutions - OneLink, AccessNow and our new Visitor Management solution Kenai.\nH\u00e5kan Bj\u00f6rkman Johan Reich Daniel Groth have led the European team with on-booth support from Spencer Marshall Amanda Morby Jason Hunter Matt Dillon (MSyl) and Matthew Wills - with Matt taking part in an expert panel session - How can technologies be combined to achieve optimal perimeter surveillance? - facilitated by Markus Lahtinen.\nThe team then topped off the week with a Gallagher Hosted Partner Dinner at Restaurang Prinsen with a celebration of partnership, success and growth in our Nordics region.\nCongratulations to the Nordics team and Amanda for another set of brilliantly delivered events in the Nordics region.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"Our Safari Social is almost here. Don\u2019t miss out on the wildest night in security.\nOur team are looking forward to welcoming security professionals, end users, consultants, and partners from across the industry to one of Toronto's most iconic venues. Whether you're looking to strengthen existing relationships or make new ones, tonight promises to be the perfect setting for collaboration, networking, and an unforgettable evening.\nCan't make it? You can still support Toronto Zoo's mission to protect and connect people, animals, and conservation science by making a donation here.\nDonate to the Toronto Zoo Community Conservation Centre: https://lnkd.in/erjttbCv","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-19","text":"We are proud to be partnering with the International Security Buyer Awards 2026!\ud83c\udfc6\nVoting is now open, and we encourage our network to have their say in recognising the people, products and innovations making an impact across the security industry.\nVOTE NOW: https://utm.guru/utph9\nRegister for your virtual seat and join us on 19 November for the live awards ceremony: https://utm.guru/utpib","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security/home/"}]}

## 2026-10-28T02:19:26Z JOHNSON
{"slug":"JOHNSON","companyName":"Johnson Controls","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28T02:19:26Z","followerCount":3810853,"bio":"Johnson Controls is a global leader in thermal management, mission-critical building systems, energy efficiency and decarbonization. We help our customers use energy more productively, reduce carbon emissions and operate with the precision and resilience required in rapidly expanding industries such as data centers, healthcare, pharmaceuticals, advanced manufacturing and higher education.\n\nFor more than 140 years, Johnson Controls has been delivering performance where it really matters. Backed by advanced technology, lifecycle services and an industry-leading field organization, we elevate customer performance, turning goals into real-world results and helping move society forward.\n\nVisit johnsoncontrols.com for more information.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"As data center demand continues to grow, owners and operators face increasing pressure to bring capacity online faster while maintaining reliability, efficiency and uptime. Reducing complexity across shipping, delivery, installation, and commissioning can accelerate time to service.\nFrom ongoing maintenance to rapid response and operational optimization, a proactive lifecycle approach helps improve resiliency and reduce risk across your critical infrastructure.\nLearn more: https://on.jci.com/4BpB3DY","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"This year, thousands of zero-day vulnerabilities were found by Anthropic, demonstrating the reality of AI-augmented attacks. Our white paper explains what this means for your OT systems\u2014and how a zero-trust overlay can protect you.\nDownload it here: https://on.jci.com/4iraDJE","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"Hidden efficiency losses happen throughout the thermal chain.\nYou\u2019re invited to join us for a webinar with Data Center Frontier on Oct. 27 at 1:00 PM EDT | Understanding Efficiency in the Thermal Chain with Bill Flaherty, Ph.D., Sr. Director, Data Center Thermal Management.\nJoin Bill as he explores how heat moves from silicon junction to CDU and where power is lost along the way.\nRegister today: https://on.jci.com/4zRPjUt","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"Don't miss this live expert panel! Join us October 27 at 12:00PM ET as we introduce the Smart Building Technology Buyer\u2019s Guide and share a practical framework for evaluating solutions, comparing vendors and building a technology roadmap that supports long-term business goals.\nCan't make it live? Register to get the recording: https://on.jci.com/4jsiKHS","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"The WLSR8000 Wireless Bus Receiver makes it easier to extend room sensing\nand control into spaces where wiring is a challenge. Providing wireless\ncommunication between NSW8000 sensors and supported Johnson Controls\ncontrollers, it fills the gap between traditional hardwired sensing and large\nenterprise wireless deployments.\nFrom retrofit projects to glass-walled offices to historic buildings, the WLSR8000\nis ideal for spaces where wiring is impractical. Expect faster installations, reduced\ndisruption for occupants and greater flexibility to adapt as building needs evolve.\nDiscover the benefits of the WLSR8000: https://on.jci.com/4yO6TYQ","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"}]}

## 2026-10-28T02:18:44Z NZPOLICE
{"slug":"NZPOLICE","companyName":"NZ Police","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/nz-police","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28T02:18:44Z","followerCount":29635,"bio":"New Zealand Police is the lead agency responsible for reducing crime and enhancing community safety. With over 15,000 staff, we provide policing services 24 hours a day and function from 371 community-based police stations around the country.\n\nWe operate by land, sea and air, and respond to more than 600,000 emergency 111 calls each year.\n\nSafer Communities Together.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"Scenario training at Scenario Village \ud83c\udfe0\nWant to see more of life at college? Check out our In Training series on YouTube - https://lnkd.in/eBs_BWVK","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/nz-police/posts/"},{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"A man who became separated from his hunting party in remote Northland bush was rescued in the early hours of Monday morning after a coordinated search effort involving Police and Land Search and Rescue.\nThe alarm was sounded around 7pm on Sunday that a member of a hunting group had gone missing in the mountainous terrain of Warawara Forest near Mitimiti.\nDetective Sergeant Ryan Cooper says the party spent several hours searching the area before notifying Police.\n\u201cWith no sign of the man, Police and Land SAR teams were deployed to the dense forest, which covers over 6800 hectares of bushland.\n\u201cA GPS dog collar provided a starting point for where he was last seen, and teams set off just after 10.30pm.\u201d\nRescuers made their way through the steep terrain, utilising sound line techniques when visual coverage was limited.\nJust after 1.30am, a successful voice appeal confirmed the man was safe and provided rescuers with his rough location.\n\u201cDense vegetation made the search challenging, with ae","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/nz-police/posts/"},{"date":"2026-10-25","text":"Lady Liz \ud83d\udc4b\n54\n\u200b\n\u200b\n\u200b\nFeed post","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/nz-police/posts/"},{"date":"2026-10-23","text":"Things you shouldn't do after a night out....\n\u274c Drive drunk\n\u274c Text your ex\nAlways drive sober or have a plan on how you will get home safely so you can end your night with no regrets.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/nz-police/posts/"},{"date":"2026-10-22","text":"The scenic route of drivers training \ud83d\ude94\n\ud83d\udccd Castlepoint\n277\n1\n2\n\u200b\nFeed post","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/nz-police/posts/"}]}

## 2026-10-28T02:18:03Z ASIS
{"slug":"ASIS","companyName":"ASIS International","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28T02:18:03Z","followerCount":102677,"bio":"The world's largest association for security professionals, ASIS International has 243 chapters around the globe. Wherever you are in your career, whether just getting started or a seasoned security professional, ASIS International has the tools, information, and global network you need to achieve your goals. Put the power of ASIS to work for you.  www.asisonline.org","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-03-05","text":"Our #MyASIS community is unmatched. We are in awe of our members\u2019 dedication to the profession and each other, who are always looking for ways to support their colleagues and friends. In honor of Membership Appreciation Month we ask that you share your appreciation for your fellow members, maybe someone who has influenced your career or helped you in your ASIS journey? Tag a member in the comments below and be entered to win a FREE GSX All-Access Pass to #GSX2026. #ASISMemberAppreciation","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"October is Cybersecurity Awareness Month, and for today\u2019s security professionals, it means something different than it did a decade ago.\nWhether your focus is corporate security, risk management, executive protection, or IT, cybersecurity now touches every discipline, and threats once confined to a single domain have far-reaching consequences.\nOn the ASIS Blog, members share how cybersecurity threats have evolved, what's next, and how to stay ahead. Read more: https://bit.ly/4z95YDg\n#CybersecurityAwarenessMonth #ASISInternational","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"Fake news that looks real. Fake job applicants who get hired. Fake authorities who walk away with confidential information.\nCybersecurity expert Tom Cross, head of threat research at GetReal Security, explains how deepfakes make it possible: AI-enabled recorded or live audio and video that looks and sounds legitimate.\nListen to the full Security Management Highlight episode here: https://bit.ly/3UEYdWw\n#ASISInternational #SecurityManagement #Deepfakes #ThreatIntelligence","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-24","text":"How are cities moving from reactive, manual investigations to real-time, data-driven public safety, and how is the same infrastructure making them smarter, not just safer?\nGet the answers from Nathan Hale and Brian Ison, CPP, CFE during ASIS\u2019s next webinar, Securing the Future: Cities Across North America.\nExpect standout moments, hard numbers, and an honest look at what separates the cities that are getting it right: open platforms, community trust, and technology deployed as part of a plan.\nFree to all | Registration required\nThursday, 29 October 2026 | 12:30 pm ET | 1 CPE\nSponsored by Milestone Systems\nRegister now: https://lnkd.in/egqk4nYr\n#SmartCity #PublicSafety #RealTimeCrime #ASISInternational","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-23","text":"Violent incidents remain low compared to previous years, but organizations aren\u2019t letting their guard down. In a new ASIS and Everbridge study, less than half of respondents  are highly or mostly confident their staff know what to do in an active assailant incident.\nThe research points to four factors linked to higher confidence in an organization\u2019s preparedness: a comprehensive plan, regular drills, communications technology, and an effective behavioral threat assessment and management (BTAM) team.\nRead the full Security Management article: https://bit.ly/4zHrXkj\nAuthor: Scott Briscoe\n#ASISInternational #ThreatAssessment #BTAM #EmergencyManagement #WorkplaceSafety","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/asis-international/home/"}]}

## 2026-10-28T02:17:22Z NZSA
{"slug":"NZSA","companyName":"New Zealand Security Association (NZSA)","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/new-zealand-security-association","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28T02:17:22Z","followerCount":3733,"bio":"The New Zealand Security Association (NZSA) is the largest industry representative body for the security industry in New Zealand and represents over 85% of the industry by revenue. Its voluntary members include security providers ranging from large multi-nationals to sole traders and also includes individuals and companies who are not direct providers of security services but have an interest in the industry.\nThe stated objective of the New Zealand Security Association is to do all things necessary and lawful to ensure there is always available to the New Zealand public, a security industry comprising of persons and firms who are fit and proper. The New Zealand Security Association is committed to the highest standards of professional and ethical conduct at all times.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"A great overview  of the 'why' behind the new New Zealand Security Association Advanced Security Officer training programme\nThanks DEFSEC New Zealand and Nicholas Dynon.\nYou can find out more about the training here, along with our good practice guidelines for citizen's arrest: https://lnkd.in/e2BZeMm6\n#CitizensArrest\n#SecurityIndustry","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/new-zealand-security-association/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"Our Advanced Security Officer training starts soon - don\u2019t forget to register to secure your place.\nHigher-risk security work demands skills beyond a CoA. NZSA\u2019s five-day Advanced Security Officer (ASO) Training Programme, incorporating citizen\u2019s arrest, helps security professionals build the practical skills and confidence needed for demanding situations.\nDeveloped with industry experts, this hands-on programme covers:\n\u2022 Legal powers, risk assessment and decision-making\n\u2022 De-escalation and safe disengagement\n\u2022 Citizen\u2019s arrest, detention and proportionate force\n\u2022 Safe intervention, restraint and welfare monitoring\n\u2022 Teamwork, Police handover, evidence and reporting\nPut your learning into practice through scenario-based assessment, with pre-assessment, certification and ongoing competency maintenance built into the programme.\n\ud83d\udcc5 Upcoming courses:\n\u2022 9\u201313 November\n\u2022 23\u201327 November\n\u2022 30 November\u20134 December\n\ud83d\udccd Epsom, Auckland | 8am\u20134pm daily\n\ud83d\udcb2 NZSA members: $1,250 + GST\n\ud83d\udcb2 Non-members: $1,500","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/new-zealand-security-association/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-19","text":"And the last (but by no means least) in our series of Security Awards winners' spotlights shines on Rick Warin. Congratulations Rick!\nView the full list of winners here: https://lnkd.in/eqUpkuCg","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/new-zealand-security-association/home/"}]}

## 2026-10-28T02:16:41Z REDWOLF
{"slug":"REDWOLF","companyName":"Red Wolf High Level Security Ltd","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/red-wolf-high-level-security-ltd","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28T02:16:41Z","followerCount":142,"bio":"Red Wolf High Level Security Ltd is a high level security integrator company based out of Wellington and Auckland, New Zealand.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"When a client reached out to us to upgrade their access control system, this wasn't just about replacing hardware.\nIt was an opportunity to create something that would be easier to maintain, easier to troubleshoot, and more reliable for years to come.\nThe before photo shows a system that's grown, changed over time, and needed more care.\nThe after photo tells the story of our craftsmanship and commitment to quality. Every cable has a place, every connection is accessible, and every component has been installed with the next technician, the next service visit, and the long-term performance of the system in mind.\nQuality isn't something that's added at the end of a project. It's built into every decision from the moment work begins.\nA huge thank you to Matthew Bowles for the care, attention to detail, and pride that went into this installation. Great results come from great craftsmanship.\n#BeforeAndAfter #Transformation #AccessControl #SecuritySystems #ProblemSolving #ContinuousImprovemen","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/red-wolf-high-level-security-ltd/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-26","text":"Happy Labour Day to every worker across New Zealand, and especially to the security professionals who help keep people, property, and communities safe.\nOur work is essential, and many in the security industry will not have the luxury of taking the day off.\nWhile others rest, travel, and spend time with loved ones, security stand ready for the next job.\nToday, we want to acknowledge and thank all Red Wolf Security employees, as well as our colleagues here in New Zealand and in Australia at ADT Security Australia, ADT Security New Zealand , Wormald NZ , ACG Integration - (Australia), Signature Security Group, Intelligent Monitoring Solutions and Intelligent Monitoring Group Limited \u2013 along with security professionals and workers around the world.\nYour commitment, professionalism, and hard work do not go unnoticed.\nIf you are fortunate enough to have the day off, we hope you enjoy it with your wh\u0101nau.\n#LabourDay #SecurityProfessionals #ProtectingWhatMatters #KeepingCommunitiesSafe #Essent","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/red-wolf-high-level-security-ltd/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-26","text":"Happy Labour Day to every worker across New Zealand, and especially to the security professionals who help keep people, property, and communities safe.\nOur work is essential, and many in the security industry will not have the luxury of taking the day off.\nWhile others rest, travel, and spend time with loved ones, security stand ready for the next job.\nToday, we want to acknowledge and thank all Red Wolf Security employees, as well as our colleagues here in New Zealand and in Australia at ADT Security Australia, ADT Security New Zealand , Wormald NZ , ACG Integration - (Australia), Signature Security Group, Intelligent Monitoring Solutions and Intelligent Monitoring Group Limited \u2013 along with security professionals and workers around the world.\nYour commitment, professionalism, and hard work do not go unnoticed.\nIf you are fortunate enough to have the day off, we hope you enjoy it with your wh\u0101nau.\n#LabourDay #SecurityProfessionals #ProtectingWhatMatters #KeepingCommunitiesSafe #Essent","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/red-wolf-high-level-security-ltd/home/","repostOf":"Red Wolf High Level Security"},{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"It's been just over a month since R. was awarded Security Consultant of the Year at the New Zealand Security Association, and we're still proud of what this achievement represents.\nCombined with Shamal Kumar's recognition as a finalist, it highlights the depth of talent across the Red Wolf team and our commitment to delivering great outcomes for our clients.\nThanks NZSA, Gary Morrison, Lucy Nichols, Tacia Strawbridge, and everyone else involved in making this incredible event possible.\nWell done again, team.\n#NZSA #SecurityAwards #TeamRedWolf #SecurityConsultant #NewZealand #RedWolfHighLevelSecurity","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/red-wolf-high-level-security-ltd/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-20","text":"What do you think is the biggest physical security gap in NZ businesses right now?\nCast your vote below, then tell us why in the comments. We'd love to hear what's happening in your industry and whether you've seen this challenge firsthand.\nWe'll publish the findings and our take next week","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/red-wolf-high-level-security-ltd/home/"}]}

## 2026-10-25T22:19:18Z JACQUES
{"slug":"JACQUES","companyName":"Jacques Technologies","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/jacques","fetchedAt":"2026-10-25T22:19:18Z","followerCount":13992,"bio":"Jacques designs and manufactures communication-critical intercom & public address products that seamlessly integrates with VMS, SMS & access control systems resulting in a complete security solution. Built initially & especially for the corrections market and with over 40 years\u2019 we\u2019re the experts in critical security communication.\n\nMore than an intercom system. Built for prisons, built to last. A Jacques IP Communication solution is built tough for critical, security communication for the corrections market, yet flexible & scalable for longevity of investment.\n\nWe are a solutions provider. We deploy communication solutions that are responsive to customer requirements and market demands. They are adaptive across many markets - hospitals, commercial buildings, education facilities including schools, industrial, smart/safe cities and transport networks.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-06-09","text":"5 days to go!\nWe're excited to see our ASBA members at the ASBA VIC chapter in Melbourne this weekend.\nIf you're attending, come visit us at stand 29\nSTAND 29\nPullman on the Park","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/jacques/home/"},{"date":"2026-05-07","text":"4 weeks to go! We're coming to Perth\nWe\u2019re excited to be exhibiting at this year\u2019s IPSHA Conference and looking forward to connecting with leaders across the education sector.\n4th - 6th June, Freemantle\n#IPSHA2026 #SchoolSafety #PublicAddress #SmartSchools","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/jacques/home/"},{"date":"2026-02-13","text":"Clear communication. Smarter security. Total reliability.\nOur latest Video Intercom System Brochure showcases how Jacques Technologies delivers high-performance audio and video communication solutions for mission-critical environments.\nDesigned for commercial buildings, healthcare, transport and public infrastructure, our systems combine crystal-clear audio, high-definition video and seamless network integration \u2014 built for projects where performance matters.\nDownload the brochure and explore how Jacques can support your next installation.\n\ud83d\udcd8 View the brochure:\nhttps://lnkd.in/g48ywq9t","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/jacques/home/"}]}

## 2026-10-25T22:18:38Z ICT
{"slug":"ICT","companyName":"Integrated Control Technology (ICT)","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology","fetchedAt":"2026-10-25T22:18:38Z","followerCount":28577,"bio":"Integrated Control Technology (ICT) is a world leading manufacturer of unified electronic access control and security solutions enabling a scalable solution for organizations to protect their people, operations and information.\n\nICT's Protege\u00ae seamlessly integrates a full suite of security management functions and technologies using an open architecture design. offering electronic access control, ID credential issuance and management; alarm monitoring, apartment management, digital video surveillance and management, real-time digital video content analysis, integration of biometric technologies, intrusion detection and smart card functionality, plus integration with a multitude of third-party systems.\n\nBased in Auckland, New Zealand, ICT has a global presence with offices located in Denver (Colorado USA), Amersham (United Kingdom), and Sydney (Australia) to provide full local sales, support and service to our clients and partners around the world.\n\nTo learn more, visit www.ict.co","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"Neil Foster and the team are back on the stand at Skydd, and day two is already off to a busy start!\nA big thank you to everyone who has stopped by so far. It's been great to show you ICT's unified, cyber-compliant platform for access control, intrusion detection and building automation.\nStop by, meet the team and get your live demo on stand A06:51. Tomorrow is the final day, so don't miss out!","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-20","text":"Day one at Skydd is underway!\nNeil Foster, our Regional Sales Director for Northern Europe, is on stand A06:51, joined by Sally Waugh and Connor Banfield.\nVisit the team for a live demonstration of ICT's unified security solution, including biometrics, intercom and CCTV integration.\nWe look forward to seeing you!\n\ud83d\udccd Stand A06:51\n\ud83d\udcc5 20\u201322 October","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-20","text":"We're exhibiting at The Security Event Asia in Singapore next month, and we're looking forward to catching up with integrators and consultants from across the region.\nYou'll find Ben Italiano and Jacky Chow on Stand 1928 at the Sands Expo & Convention Centre from 10 to 12 November, along with demonstrations in how ICT Protege GX secures sites across the banking, logistics and technology sectors.\n#TSEAsia #ICT","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-20","text":"This week, we\u2019re heading to Security Canada Central and we want to hear about your toughest sites.\nMore doors. More users. More systems. More moving parts that all need to work together.\nComplex sites don\u2019t need more complexity. With Protege GX, access control, intrusion detection and building automation come together on one unified platform, with integrations to the video, intercom and business systems your customers already rely on.\nThe result? Fewer systems to manage, less complexity and a solution built to scale with your customers.\n\ud83d\udccd Find the ICT team at Booth 523\n\ud83d\udcc5 October 21\u201322\nBring us your toughest security challenge. We\u2019d love to talk through how Protege GX can simplify it.\n#ICT #SecurityCanadaCentral #AcccessControl #ProtegeGX","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-22","text":"When we think high security, we often think of banks.\nTheir brick-and-mortar branches must be capable of protecting both staff and assets in an instant.\nProtege GX secures banks across New Zealand, Asia and Canada.\nA teller can raise a silent duress alarm without anyone noticing, the vault opens only for two authorised people and each branch keeps running when the network drops. You can move a bank off its legacy cards one branch at a time, with access control, intrusion detection and building automation on one platform.\nWorking on a banking project?\nTalk it through at Stand 1928, Singapore, 10 to 12 November.\n#TSEAsia #ICT","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"}]}

## 2026-10-25T22:17:57Z BOSCH
{"slug":"BOSCH","companyName":"Bosch Security and Safety Systems","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/bosch-security-systems","fetchedAt":"2026-10-25T22:17:57Z","followerCount":46452,"bio":"This LinkedIn page for Bosch Security and Safety Systems is no longer active.\nThe business has been acquired by Triton and is now part of the Keenfinity Group, an independent company delivering professional communication and security solutions that connect and protect people and assets. Keenfinity Group combines leading brands and expertise across Audio, Video Systems, Intrusion & Access, and Electronics Manufacturing Services (EMS), serving customers worldwide.\n\nTo continue receiving product updates, insights, and news, please follow our dedicated LinkedIn pages: \n\u2022 Video Systems: IQSIGHT https://www.linkedin.com/company/iqsight\n\u2022 Intrusion & Access: Radionix https://www.linkedin.com/company/radionix\n\u2022 Conference Solutions | Keenfinity Group https://www.linkedin.com/company/bosch-conference-solutions\n\u2022 Public Address & Voice Alarm | Keenfinity Group https://www.linkedin.com/company/public-address-solutions\n\nMore information: www.keenfinity-group.com","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-07-01","text":"\u203c\ufe0fImportant update\u203c\ufe0f\nThis LinkedIn page Bosch Security and Safety Systems is no longer active.\nTo continue receiving updates and insights on our products, please follow our dedicated LinkedIn pages that are now part of Keenfinity Group:\n\u00b7\u00a0Video Systems \ud83d\udc49 IQSIGHT\n\u00b7\u00a0Intrusion & Access Systems \ud83d\udc49 Radionix\n\u00b7\u00a0Conference Solutions \ud83d\udc49 Conference solutions | Keenfinity Group\n\u00b7\u00a0Public Address Systems \ud83d\udc49 Public Address & Voice Alarm | Keenfinity Group\nThank you for being part of our community here. We look forward to staying connected with you on LinkedIn.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/bosch-security-systems/home/"},{"date":"2026-06-30","text":"Trusted worldwide. Built for what matters.\nThe transition from Bosch Video Systems to IQSIGHT is officially complete.\nWhile our name has changed, the foundation remains the same: more than 60 years of engineering excellence, trusted products, global expertise, and a commitment to helping organizations operate safely, securely, and without interruption.\nFrom everyday operations to mission-critical environments, we deliver reliable, intelligence-first video solutions that perform.\nWelcome to the next chapter. Stay connected with us here > https://lnkd.in/gjd8fz9U","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/bosch-security-systems/home/"},{"date":"2026-06-29","text":"Final reminder: Public Address and Voice Alarm content continues on our dedicated page.\nThis will be our final PAVA-related post on this channel!\nFrom now on, Public Address and Voice Alarm content will continue on the dedicated Public Address & Voice Alarm LinkedIn page.\nThe page is active, focused and built for technical consultants, system integrators, specifiers, project engineers and other professionals working with PAVA systems.\nThank you for following the PAVA conversation here. We look forward to continuing it with you on the dedicated page. See you there?\n\ud83d\udc49 https://lnkd.in/dDcDKfU7\n#BoschPublicAddress #PRAESENSA #PublicAddressandVoiceAlarm #VoiceAlarm #Countdown","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/bosch-security-systems/home/"},{"date":"2026-06-24","text":"We're moving all Conference Systems updates to our \ud835\uddf1\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddf1\ud835\uddf6\ud835\uddf0\ud835\uddee\ud835\ude01\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddf1 #Conference Solutions \ud835\udddf\ud835\uddf6\ud835\uddfb\ud835\uddf8\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddf1\ud835\udddc\ud835\uddfb \ud835\uddfd\ud835\uddee\ud835\uddf4\ud835\uddf2.\nBy following our conference solutions page, you'll receive updates on audio innovation, meeting management, industry trends, events, and product developments, all in one place.\nNo unrelated content. Just