## 2026-10-25T22:17:16Z INNERRANGE
{"slug":"INNERRANGE","companyName":"Inner Range ANZ","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/inner-range-anz","fetchedAt":"2026-10-25T22:17:16Z","followerCount":3153,"bio":"Inner Range is a manufacturer of integrated Video, Access Control and Security solutions. Founded in Melbourne, Australia, Inner Range has over 35 years of innovation and has more than 150,000 systems deployed globally.\n \nWe are passionate about empowering our customers to protect what they value most, their property, their possessions and most importantly \u2013 their people.\n \nWe manufacture end-to-end solutions from the card you badge at one of our readers to the controller securing the door, right through to the enterprise security management software monitoring multiple sites anywhere in the world. Our scalable products are suitable for high-end residential, commercial and enterprise sites across verticals such as education, healthcare, government and critical infrastructure.\n \nOur continual investment in research and development puts our products at the forefront of access control, security, video and smart building technology. We partner with best-in-class providers of adjacent technologies such as intercom, payroll, building automation and incorporate the latest in AI technology with solutions for facial recognition, biometrics, number plate recognition and many more. With over 120 native integrations to 3rd party systems and open integration pathways, we provide our customers with a unified system behind a single pane of glass.\n \nInner Range offers our partners a range of competency-based training courses to ensure the best experience with our products and outcomes for their customers. Additionally, our global support team ensures that any issues are resolved quickly with minimal impact to the end user.\n \nFrom entry to enterprise, Inner Range provides an end-to-end security solution capable of addressing the most difficult building management needs, providing peace of mind for you and your people.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"Join Inner Range Global at the Security & Government Expo (SAGE) 2026 and discover how government, defence, and critical infrastructure organisations are strengthening security with a unified platform for access control, automation, and real-time monitoring.\nBuilt for high-security environments, Inner Range has been protecting government, defence, and critical infrastructure for over a decade. Our Class 5 certified Infiniti security platform delivers advanced access control, encrypted intrusion detection, unified video surveillance, and real-time monitoring, which provide optimal security protection.\nSee the latest innovations in Integriti and learn how Inner Range helps organisations improve security, streamline operations, and gain greater control across complex environments.\nThursday 19 November 2026 | Booth 28\nHotel Realm, Canberra\nEvent Info: https://lnkd.in/ekyJ_bMA\nWe look forward to connecting with security professionals and discussing the future of high-security management sol","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/inner-range-anz/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-22","text":"We had a fantastic first day at the CANASA Central security show. Come on in and chat with the Inner Range Global team and the team from Omni-Tech Solution Services about our unified and integrated access, video and intrusion solutions that span from entry level single site right up to enterprise grade multisite deployments.\nLive demo's, great conversations, broaden your horizons.\nCatch us tomorrow at booth 1030 before it's all over for another year.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/inner-range-anz/home/","repostOf":"Inner Range North America"},{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"Inner Range Global has released IR Connect 3.9.0, featuring interface enhancements, a new camera search function and performance improvements designed to deliver an enhanced mobile security experience.\nKey Highlights:\n- Refined interface enhancements for improved usability and navigation\n- New camera search functionality for quickly locating cameras across large deployments\n- Enhanced performance for a smoother user experience\n- Instant access to cameras, alarms and critical events\n- Real-time notifications and updates\n- Available on Android and iOS devices\nFor more info: https://lnkd.in/eNdeNh8q\nWhether you're managing a single site or a multi-site enterprise, IR Connect keeps you connected to your security system whenever and wherever it's needed.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/inner-range-anz/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-02","text":"Secure. Resilient. Always Connected.\nMeet the Inner Range T4000 Pro \u2013 the most advanced communicator in the Inner Range portfolio, designed to keep your security systems online when it matters most.\n- Integrated 4G LTE, Ethernet & Wi-Fi routing\n- Dual-SIM automatic failover\n- Secure VPN support (WireGuard & OpenVPN)\n- Reliable video streaming\n- High-speed alarm communication\n- Centralised remote device management\nWhen primary internet connectivity fails, the T4000 Pro automatically switches to 4G, ensuring uninterrupted alarm reporting, video transmission, and remote access.\nFor More Information: https://lnkd.in/edz9ZbhW\n#InnerRange #T4000Pro #SecurityTechnology #AlarmCommunication #RemoteMonitoring #AccessControl #VideoSurveillance #SecuritySystems","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/inner-range-anz/home/"}]}

## 2026-10-25T22:16:36Z GALLAGHER
{"slug":"GALLAGHER","companyName":"Gallagher Security","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security","fetchedAt":"2026-10-25T22:16:36Z","followerCount":33440,"bio":"Gallagher Security is a global leader in integrated technology solutions that help organizations around the world protect, secure, and manage people and assets. Our award-winning solutions are trusted by government, defense, commercial, industrial, healthcare, transportation, mining, and educational organizations in 140 countries.\n\nWe design and manufacture a comprehensive suite of security software and hardware - including integrated access control, intruder alarm, and perimeter solutions - all on site at our global headquarters. The intelligent technology can be scaled and customized to deliver business efficiencies across simple, enterprise, and high security sites.\n\nTrusted by over 20,000 security customers worldwide, Gallagher solutions are used to simplify life on campus within the education sector, keep staff and patients safe in healthcare, ensure the highest security requirements and compliances are met for government sites in the Five Eyes alliance, safeguard critical infrastructure within the utilities industry, and ensure uninterrupted movement for transport and logistics.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"Our Safari Social is almost here. Don\u2019t miss out on the wildest night in security.\nOur team are looking forward to welcoming security professionals, end users, consultants, and partners from across the industry to one of Toronto's most iconic venues. Whether you're looking to strengthen existing relationships or make new ones, tonight promises to be the perfect setting for collaboration, networking, and an unforgettable evening.\nCan't make it? You can still support Toronto Zoo's mission to protect and connect people, animals, and conservation science by making a donation here.\nDonate to the Toronto Zoo Community Conservation Centre: https://lnkd.in/erjttbCv","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-23","text":"#SKYDD and #TeamGallagher in Stockholm for an incredible 3 days of networking and connection to showcase our Gallagher Security solutions - OneLink, AccessNow and our new Visitor Management solution Kenai.\nH\u00e5kan Bj\u00f6rkman Johan Reich Daniel Groth have led the European team with on-booth support from Spencer Marshall Amanda Morby Jason Hunter Matt Dillon (MSyl) and Matthew Wills - with Matt taking part in an expert panel session - How can technologies be combined to achieve optimal perimeter surveillance? - facilitated by Markus Lahtinen.\nThe team then topped off the week with a Gallagher Hosted Partner Dinner at Restaurang Prinsen with a celebration of partnership, success and growth in our Nordics region.\nCongratulations to the Nordics team and Amanda for another set of brilliantly delivered events in the Nordics region.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-19","text":"We are proud to be partnering with the International Security Buyer Awards 2026!\ud83c\udfc6\nVoting is now open, and we encourage our network to have their say in recognising the people, products and innovations making an impact across the security industry.\nVOTE NOW: https://utm.guru/utph9\nRegister for your virtual seat and join us on 19 November for the live awards ceremony: https://utm.guru/utpib","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-16","text":"SMB just got smarter.\nNew Self-service Access Schedules mean routine door changes happen instantly, no installer callout needed. And Duress Code gives users a quiet way to signal for help during normal entry.\nReal updates, real impact.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/gallagher-security/home/"}]}

## 2026-10-25T22:15:55Z JOHNSON
{"slug":"JOHNSON","companyName":"Johnson Controls","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls","fetchedAt":"2026-10-25T22:15:55Z","followerCount":3808612,"bio":"Johnson Controls is a global leader in thermal management, mission-critical building systems, energy efficiency and decarbonization. We help our customers use energy more productively, reduce carbon emissions and operate with the precision and resilience required in rapidly expanding industries such as data centers, healthcare, pharmaceuticals, advanced manufacturing and higher education.\n\nFor more than 140 years, Johnson Controls has been delivering performance where it really matters. Backed by advanced technology, lifecycle services and an industry-leading field organization, we elevate customer performance, turning goals into real-world results and helping move society forward.\n\nVisit johnsoncontrols.com for more information.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-23","text":"Last chance to take advantage of the Facility Explorer\u00ae FX90 license transfer offer!\nTime is running out to upgrade from FX80 to the next generation of Facility Explorer; the license transfer promotion ends October 31.\nUpgrade to FX90 to:\n\u2714 Reduce risk\n\u2714 Avoid obsolescence\n\u2714 Maintain future connectivity and support\nDon't miss the opportunity to modernize your building automation system while taking advantage of this limited-time offer.\nGet the details now: https://ow.ly/M19v50ZQjRX","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-23","text":"Smart building technology is evolving fast. Is your technology strategy keeping pace? \ud83c\udfc3\u200d\u2642\ufe0f\nJoin us October 27 at 12:00PM ET as we introduce the Smart Building Technology Buyer\u2019s Guide and share a practical framework for evaluating solutions, comparing vendors and building a technology roadmap that supports long-term business goals.\nFrom AI and cybersecurity to integration and data intelligence, learn what to look for and what questions to ask before making your next technology investment.\nRegister now: https://on.jci.com/4jsiKHS","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-22","text":"Cyber resilience starts by improving your system's visibility, reducing risk and prioritizing modernization. Our on-demand webinar gives you a strategy to do all three and secure your connected buildings. Get our experts' advice and move from awareness to action by watching it now: https://on.jci.com/4yyRsmR","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-22","text":"As AI reshapes data center requirements, cooling decisions are increasingly connected to the broader design strategy.\nHigher rack densities can affect everything from infrastructure planning to efficiency and long-term flexibility, making thermal management a key consideration in the design process.\nExplore what this shift means for AI data centers: https://on.jci.com/4B9mMv3","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-24","text":"Realizing the potential of AI at scale requires infrastructure capable of supporting unprecedented levels of compute, power and cooling. We\u2019re proud to work with Armada and NVIDIA to help advance the critical infrastructure needed for the next generation of AI factories.\nTogether, we\u2019re helping\u00a0solve some of the most important constraints to scaling AI and bringing new capacity online faster.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/johnson-controls/home/"}]}

