security executive, risk leader, or operational manager, staying ahead of legislative change is a strategic necessity.\nTo make sense of it all, we\u2019ve put together an exclusive dual-keynote lineup:\n\ud83c\udfa4 Hon. Mark Mitchell \u2013 Minister for Police, Corrections, and Emergency Management. Bringing direct insights into recent legislative changes, policy shifts, and national saf","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/new-zealand-security-association/home/"}]}

## 2026-10-25T22:13:13Z REDWOLF
{"slug":"REDWOLF","companyName":"Red Wolf High Level Security Ltd","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/red-wolf-high-level-security-ltd","fetchedAt":"2026-10-25T22:13:13Z","followerCount":134,"bio":"Red Wolf High Level Security Ltd is a high level security integrator company based out of Wellington and Auckland, New Zealand.","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-25","text":"Happy Labour Day to every worker across New Zealand, and especially to the security professionals who help keep people, property, and communities safe.\nOur work is essential, and many in the security industry will not have the luxury of taking the day off.\nWhile others rest, travel, and spend time with loved ones, security stand ready for the next job.\nToday, we want to acknowledge and thank all Red Wolf Security employees, as well as our colleagues here in New Zealand and in Australia at ADT Security Australia, ADT Security New Zealand , Wormald NZ , ACG Integration - (Australia), Signature Security Group, Intelligent Monitoring Solutions and Intelligent Monitoring Group Limited \u2013 along with security professionals and workers around the world.\nYour commitment, professionalism, and hard work do not go unnoticed.\nIf you are fortunate enough to have the day off, we hope you enjoy it with your wh\u0101nau.\n#LabourDay #SecurityProfessionals #ProtectingWhatMatters #KeepingCommunitiesSafe #Essent","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/red-wolf-high-level-security-ltd/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"It's been just over a month since R. was awarded Security Consultant of the Year at the New Zealand Security Association, and we're still proud of what this achievement represents.\nCombined with Shamal Kumar's recognition as a finalist, it highlights the depth of talent across the Red Wolf team and our commitment to delivering great outcomes for our clients.\nThanks NZSA, Gary Morrison, Lucy Nichols, Tacia Strawbridge, and everyone else involved in making this incredible event possible.\nWell done again, team.\n#NZSA #SecurityAwards #TeamRedWolf #SecurityConsultant #NewZealand #RedWolfHighLevelSecurity","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/red-wolf-high-level-security-ltd/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-20","text":"What do you think is the biggest physical security gap in NZ businesses right now?\nCast your vote below, then tell us why in the comments. We'd love to hear what's happening in your industry and whether you've seen this challenge firsthand.\nWe'll publish the findings and our take next week","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/red-wolf-high-level-security-ltd/home/"},{"date":"2026-09-12","text":"Well done to our very own Reck R. for winning security consultant of the year at the New Zealand Security Association awards night last night, definitely deserved! Also a huge congratulations to Shamal Kumar from our team for being a finalist also! Well done team! Congratulations to everyone who won awards and finalists!","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/red-wolf-high-level-security-ltd/home/"},{"date":"2026-08-12","text":"Well done team!\nReck R.\n\u2022 3rd+\nSRMP\u2013C | Security Consultant of the Year (2026)\nBook an appointment\nAug 12 \u2022 Edited\nThe day started with fantastic news! I\u2019m proud to share that Shamal Kumar and I have been selected as finalists for the New Zealand Security Association Awards.\n\u200bA h-u-g-e thank you to our incredible team at Red Wolf High Level Security and the executive at ASIS New Zealand for enabling me to do my work.\n\u200bMore than anyone else, I want to thank my partner, Jay R. , for helping me become a better person on both a personal and professional level.\n\u200b\nCongrats to Shamal and all the other finalists. Looking forward to the awards night!\nCustomer Champion\nChelsea Wallis \u2013 Optic Security Group\nRebecca Magee \u2013 Armourguard Security\nSu Kaur \u2013 FIRST Security\nDesign and Support Electronic Sector Professional\nBartho Huyser \u2013 Optic Security\nDaniel Malan \u2013 Global Security Solutions Limited Ltd\nSimon Paul \u2013 ICE Security Limited\nElectronic Security Trainee\nBrynn Lightfoot \u2013 Nelson Alarms Secu","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/red-wolf-high-level-security-ltd/home/"}]}
